=== family_ages ===

Ages #title

$image lesson2-family-ages.jpg

This is the Smith family.
There are five people in the family.

Mr. and Mrs. Smith are the parents.
John, Helen, and Emma are the children.

John is twelve years old.
Helen is ten years old.
Emma is six months old.

John is the oldest child.
Helen is younger than John.
Emma is the youngest child.
Emma is also the baby.

How old is John?
* [He is twelve.] #ok
* [He is ten.] #fail
* [He is six months old.] #fail
-

John is twelve years old.

How old is Helen?
* [She is ten.] #ok
* [She is twelve.] #fail
* [She is six months old.] #fail
-

Helen is ten years old.

How old is Emma?
* [She is six months old.] #ok
* [She is six years old.] #fail
* [She is ten years old.] #fail
-

Emma is six months old.

$image lesson2-ages-chart.jpg

John is two years older than Helen.
Helen is two years younger than John.

Is Helen older than John?
* [No, she is younger.] #ok
* [Yes, she is older.] #fail
-

Helen is younger than John.

Is Emma younger than Helen?
* [Yes, she is.] #ok
* [No, she is older.] #fail
-

Emma is younger than Helen.
Emma is the youngest of the three children.

Mr. Smith is thirty-six years old.
Mrs. Smith is thirty-two years old.
Mr. Smith's father is sixty-three years old.

He is John's grandfather.
The grandfather is older than everyone in the family.

$image lesson2-family-ages-all.jpg

Who is the oldest person in the family?
* [John's grandfather.] #ok
* [Mrs. Smith.] #fail
* [John.] #fail
-

John's grandfather is the oldest person in the family.

Do Mr. and Mrs. Smith have three children?
* [Yes, they do.] #ok
* [No, they have two.] #fail
-

They have three children.

Do they have one son and two daughters?
* [Yes, they do.] #ok
* [No, they have two sons.] #fail
-

They have one son and two daughters.

Dialogue.

@mrs_smith John, how old are you?
@john I am twelve years old.
@mrs_smith And how old is Helen?
@john She is ten years old.
@mr_smith Who is the youngest child?
@helen Emma is the youngest child. She is only six months old.
